AI-19 security and no-claim proof

Checked by schema/tests and rendered proof:

- No raw child copy is claimed.
- No shaming or surveillance copy is claimed.
- Rendered warning/block/approval/limited/checking states require adapter proof refs.
- The rendered pages are served from a local child-agent endpoint using the
  shared renderer output file hook.
- The script uses an isolated Chrome proof profile and does not attach to a
  personal/default browser profile.

No-claim boundaries:

- No unmanaged exact URL evidence.
- No native app or native game control.
- No cloud-stream frame analysis.
- No connector authorization.
- No final policy execution.
- No enforcement claim.
